# Dockerfile.api.dockerignore — build context for the API serving image.
#
# BuildKit uses this file INSTEAD OF the root .dockerignore when building with
# `-f Dockerfile.api` (it does not merge with it), so this file is deliberately
# self-contained.
#
# Strategy: deny everything, then re-include only what Dockerfile.api copies.
# The repository working tree is several hundred megabytes (mlruns/, DVC cache,
# processed data, .venv); an allow-list keeps all of it out by construction
# rather than by remembering to add each new exclusion.
#
# The API serves in BUNDLE mode: it needs the checksum-verified deployment
# bundle and nothing else.  No dataset, no MLflow database, no mlruns/, no DVC
# metadata, and no credential file ever enters this context.

# ── Deny everything ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**

# ── Re-include only what the image needs ─────────────────────────────────────
# Inference and application source
!src/
# Runtime configuration read by src/config.py
!params.yaml
# Package metadata for `pip install --no-deps -e .`
!pyproject.toml
# Dependency pins for the build stage.  Only the inference runtime manifest is
# admitted — the full development requirements.txt never enters this context, so
# the image cannot accidentally install MLflow/DVC/Evidently/Streamlit.
!requirements-api.txt
# Container entrypoint helpers (init_mlflow.sh, init_drift.sh)
!docker/
# Checksum-verified champion bundle — the only model artifact in the image
!deploy/bundles/

# ── Re-exclude anything unwanted that the rules above would pull back in ─────
# Caches and build residue under src/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.so
**/*.egg-info/
# Secrets must never enter the context, under any circumstances
.env
**/.env
.dvc/
.dvc/config.local
*.pem
*.key
# Editor and OS noise
**/.DS_Store
**/*.swp
